    {
      "unit_id": "qrm-acceptance-sampling-oc-curve-a47b09353043:p0009:text",
      "course_id": "qrm",
      "document_id": "qrm-acceptance-sampling-oc-curve-a47b09353043",
      "kind": "page_text",
      "text": "Single Sampling Plan\n\nProcess: Take one random sample of size n from the lot.\n  Count the number of nonconforming items.\n   If the count is less than or equal to the acceptance\n    number c, accept the lot.\n   If the count exceeds c, reject the lot.\nAdvantages: Simple to administer and requires relatively\n  straightforward calculation.\nDisadvantages: May require more inspected items on\n  average compared to other plans, especially when the lots\n  are of consistently good quality.",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "slide": 9,
        "bbox": null
      },
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "Acceptance_Sampling_OC_Curve_ME327E.pdf",
