      "kind": "page_text",
      "text": "Sequential Sampling Plan\n\nProcess: Inspect items one at a time and after each, decide\n   to accept, reject, or inspect more.\n  Uses a graph (acceptance and rejection lines) plotting\n     cumulative nonconforming items against items\n     inspected to decide when to stop.\nAdvantages:\n  Can minimize inspection efforts—potentially leading to\n     very few items needing inspection when quality level is\n      clearly good or bad.\nDisadvantages:\n  Most mathematically complex, and requires constant\n     record-keeping during inspection.",
